  "answer": "The authors split the task of applying SSL with agents into two sub-problems: (1) program discovery, where an agent iteratively generates and refines candidate programs under limited feedback, and (2) program selection, where a single program must be identified from the discovered candidates for deployment under label scarcity [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p4:para350:9].",
