  "answer": "Oracle performance, when assessing program discovery, is defined as the test performance of the best program in the discovered pool, denoted as Q(A∗). This measure evaluates the quality of the best discovered solution, independent of the ability to select it [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p5:para350:3].",
