 {
  "query_id": "q08",
  "split": "dev",
  "answerable": true,
  "question": "Why can metrics based on learned representations fail to tell agent-generated programs apart?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "Metrics based on learned representations can fail to distinguish between agent-generated programs because the agent may utilize the same frozen representation while employing different downstream self-supervised learning (SSL) procedures. This means that even if there are significant differences in predictive performance, representation-based metrics may not be able to differentiate between the programs effectively [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p7:para350:5]. Additionally, these metrics encode assumptions about what constitutes a good model, which can limit their effectiveness in unsupervised selection contexts [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p7:para350:4].",
